ick, the other copy likely picks too, though their inputs differ slightly. I'm also thinking about how partial similarity, weighted by lambda, changes the payoffs for cooperating versus defecting.\n\nI'm working out the expected payoffs for cooperating versus defecting, weighting the correlated and independent cases by lambda. Under independence defecting always gains 2, while under correlation cooperating comes out ahead by 2, so cooperating wins once lambda passes 0.5. Since the copies share a model and face a symmetric problem, I'll treat lambda as high and go with cooperation.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8348,"completion_tokens":430,"total_tokens":8778,"cost":0.041992,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.041992,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.033392,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0086},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":307,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}